-- Migration 090 — One-time data import: ServiceM8 bundle catalog
-- Already applied directly via Supabase MCP execute_sql on 2026-09-07 - this
-- file is kept for the record, not meant to be re-run (materials/prebuilds
-- have no natural unique key to make it idempotent - running it again would
-- duplicate everything).
--
-- Source: Jasper exported SM8's Bundles Catalog (55 bundles, 324 component
-- mapping rows, 182 referenced materials). A separate chat session cleaned
-- it into Thomson_Bundles_Cleaned.xlsx - alternates removed (only the
-- selected qty>0 option per slot kept), labour consolidated from 5 SM8 rate
-- identifiers down to one "Licensed Electrical Specialist" line per bundle,
-- Contingency/Sundries kept as flat markup lines. See
-- PROJECT_SPEC.md A9/A9a for what's built and what's still open (67
-- materials tagged "Other / Needs Review" need a manual categorisation
-- pass; one switch bundle's default material was auto-picked as the
-- cheapest of 14 uncategorised SM8 options and needs Jasper's confirmation).
--
-- 8 pseudo-"materials" that were really labour rates or markup placeholders
-- (COMM LABOUR, CONTINGENCY, 2/3/4 - Labour, NEWBLD LABOUR, RESI LABOUR,
-- SUNDRIES) were deliberately excluded from the materials import - they got
-- collapsed into prebuild_components directly instead (labour -> the real
-- billable_rate_tiers "Licensed Electrical Specialist" rate, which happened
-- to already exist at exactly 122.73, an exact match to SM8's own rate;
-- markup -> flat per-bundle lines), since they aren't real purchasable
-- stock and don't belong in a materials/purchasing database.
--
-- Materials: 174 rows
