('e53a0b08-85ee-496e-8770-45af737becac', 'ELCM', NULL, '(RESIDENTIAL) INSTALL NEW CONSUMER MAINS IN CONDUIT (PER METER) - Measure and cut a new aperture suitable for the new power circuit in conduit. Supply and install the appropriate cabling and terminations. Supply and install the new power circuit in conduit as required; meeting the manufacturer''s specifications.', 'Electrical', NULL, now()),
('48442855-1b5e-4944-b902-aed99fb270ba', 'Lighting track', NULL, 'Supply and Installation of Lighting Track – Determine suitable mounting locations and layout to achieve specified illumination and flexibility. Supply and install track system, including all required mounting hardware, cabling, supports, and terminations. Ensure track is securely fixed, aligned, and ready for connection. All works to be carried out in accordance with manufacturer’s specifications and all relevant Australian Standards and regulations.', 'Electrical', NULL, now()),
('5bd878db-c7f8-4058-ad0a-a9bb8c25e0c4', 'ELINSII', NULL, 'INSTALL NEW SOLAR INVERTER INSTALLATION - Measure and cut a new aperture suitable for the new Solar Inverter Installation. Supply and install the appropriate cabling and terminations. Supply and install the new Solar Inverter Installation as required; meeting the manufacturer''s specifications.', 'Electrical', NULL, now()),
('95b06331-4325-4066-9e32-92d60fe4fc2b', 'SOL-DR-10', NULL, '(SOLAR) DISCONNECT, REMOVE & REINSTALL PANELS (ROOF REPLACEMENT)
Disconnect and isolate the solar system safely at the inverter. Remove all solar panels and mounting rail from the affected roof section and store securely on site. Once the roofer has completed the roofing works, reinstall the panels using the existing rail, cabling and panels, and recommission the system.
Price includes up to 10 panels.
No allowance for additional or replacement materials (rail, cabling, panels or mounting hardware).', 'Electrical', NULL, now()),
('2b6a882b-d660-4f2d-b813-d5c1ca2ebabb', 'EINWL', NULL, '(RESIDENTIAL) INSTALL NEW WALL LIGHT UP/DOWN - Measure and cut a new aperture suitable for the new Wall Light. Supply and install the appropriate cabling and terminations. Supply and install the new Wall Light as required; meeting the manufacturer''s specifications.', 'Electrical', NULL, now()),
